    "result_text": "All 33 tests pass, including the new `Cp22Tests`, and the build succeeds.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `bulkSignupWarning` rule for `POST /api/owners`: the response now includes `bulkSignupWarning: true` when more than 80 owners had already been created today (same registration date), otherwise `false`. Like the existing `namesakeCount`/`customerCode` derived fields, it's snapshotted at creation time and read back via `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\nChanges made:\n\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 set `owner.setBulkSignupWarning(createdToday > 80)`, reusing the same `createdToday` count already computed for the daily-limit (`>= 100`) rule. It's evaluated before the current owner is saved, so it reflects owners *already* created today.\n- **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `bulkSignupWarning` (`Boolean`) persistent field mapped to column `bulk_signup_warning`, with getter/setter.\n- **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `bulkSignupWarning` boolean property to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it (MapStruct auto-maps it by name).\n- **DB schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `postgres`, `mysql`) \u2014 added the `bulk_signup_warning` column (`BOOLEAN`, `BIT(1)` for MySQL). Tests run under `hsqldb` with `ddl-auto=none`, so the schema.sql column is required.\n\nThe specified test asserts the `false` branch for a fresh create; the `> 80` branch rides the same daily-registration accumulation path as the existing per-day cap rule.",
